# What Wave A changed that shows on a real VT: the blink styles (#81),
# X11 color names in OSC color specs (#103), and a program waking the
# blank (#79). Run it with partial blink and blinking decorations, so the
# new behaviour is on screen:
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=wave-a DEMO_ARGS='--blink-text=partial --blink-decorations'

title: Wave A on a real display

step: Partial blink dims instead of hiding, and stays smooth
run: printf '\033[5mblink\033[0m \033[5;4mblink-under\033[0m \033[5;9;31mblink-red\033[0m steady\n'
do: watch the line for a few seconds, closely, at your normal viewing
do: distance.
expect: blink, blink-under and blink-red pulse between full and about half
expect: brightness, never vanishing; the underline and the strike pulse
expect: with their text; steady never changes; the cursor blinks as before.
expect: The dimmed phase is an even, readable half-tone with no flicker,
expect: banding or ghosting of the glyph edges.

step: X11 color names set the colors
run: printf '\033]11;dark slate gray\a\033]10;Gold\a\033]4;1;Light Sea Green\a\033[31mindex one\033[0m\n'
expect: the background turns dark slate gray and the default text gold,
expect: at once; "index one" is drawn light sea green.

step: The colors return
run: printf '\033]104\a\033]110\a\033]111\a'
expect: the background, the default text and color 1 return to their
expect: configured colors, with nothing left of the previous step.

step: A program wakes the blank
run: printf '\033[9;1]'; sleep 75; printf '\033[13]'
do: after Enter, touch no key or the pointer until the question below the
do: command comes back.
expect: the screen goes dark about a minute after Enter, and lights again
expect: about 15 seconds later with no key pressed, this screen drawn
expect: whole, then the question.

step: Colored underlines in every style, and the strike
run: printf '\033[4:1;58:2::255:0:0msingle\033[0m \033[4:2;58:2::0:200:0mdouble\033[0m \033[4:3;58:2::0:128:255mcurly\033[0m \033[4:4;58:5:208mdotted\033[0m \033[4:5;58:5:201mdashed\033[0m \033[9mstrike\033[0m \033[9;4:3;58:5:226mboth\033[0m\n'
expect: single in red, double in green, curly in blue, dotted in orange
expect: and dashed in magenta, each in its own style under white text;
expect: strike struck through in the text's color; both carries a yellow
expect: curly underline and a strike, each telling apart from the other.

step: Anything else
do: look over the session as a whole.
expect: nothing looks wrong: note anything that does, however small.
